---
import DocsLayout from "@/layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import heroImg from "@/assets/hero.png"
import { Code } from 'astro-expressive-code/components'
---

<DocsLayout title="Installation">
  <h1>Installation</h1>
    <p class="muted">
    Writer is cross-plaform. The repository <a href="https://github.com/git-emran/simple-notes">Github</a> includes build scripts for macOS/Windows/Linux.
    </p>

  <Code code={`git clone github.com/git-emran/simple-notes.git`} lang="bash"/>

  <h2>Step 1: Install Dependencies</h2>
    <p>If You are using `npm` or `yarn` run npm or yarn install </p>
    <Code code={`npm install`} lang="bash"/>

  <h2>Step 2: Build script</h2>
    <p>To build run the following command:</p>
    <Code code={`npm run build`} lang="bash"/>
    <p>To get an executable run the following command, which is available on the `dist` folder.</p>
    <Code code={`npm run package:mac`} lang="bash"/>
</DocsLayout>
